Found while replaying the karr #101 AKI captures 2026-08-24; verified offline against df531dd.

Langertha::Response.cached_tokens documents itself (Response.pm:367) as the engine-agnostic
"cached prompt tokens as the provider reports it". It is populated in exactly two places, both
OpenAI-shaped:

  Role::OpenAICompatible::chat_response  <- usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens
  Response.pm:409-415 (BUILDARGS lift)   <- usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens

The Anthropic wire reports the same quantity as usage.cache_read_input_tokens.
Role::AnthropicCompatible::chat_response never maps it. Result on a real captured body:

  AKIAnthropic  usage {input_tokens 64, output_tokens 2, cache_read_input_tokens 48}
                -> $response->cached_tokens = undef
  AKIOpenAI     usage {..., prompt_tokens_details {cached_tokens 48}}
                -> $response->cached_tokens = 48

Same provider, same prompt, same 48 cached tokens, one number visible and one not, purely
by which shim answered. Affects all five AnthropicCompatible consumers -- Anthropic itself,
MiniMaxAnthropic, MoonshotAnthropic, AKIAnthropic, LMStudioAnthropic. The real Anthropic
engine is the one that matters most: prompt caching is a headline feature there and
ADR 0009 gives it a first-class request-side surface, so the response side reading undef is
a visible gap in the pair.

The value is NOT lost -- it survives verbatim inside ->usage, and t/91_response_usage.t:281
asserts exactly that. But that test locks in usage passthrough and never asks about
cached_tokens, which is why the gap has been invisible.

Suggested fix: map usage.cache_read_input_tokens -> cached_tokens in
Role::AnthropicCompatible::chat_response (or extend the Response BUILDARGS lift to know both
wire spellings -- decide which layer owns it; the BUILDARGS lift already sets the precedent).
Open question for whoever takes it: cache_creation_input_tokens is a different quantity
(write, not read) and should NOT be folded in.

Fixtures available from the #101 run, both carrying real nonzero values:
  akianthropic_chat_response.json       cache_read_input_tokens 48
  akianthropic_tool_call_response.json  cache_read_input_tokens 192

Fixed in 196a274: Response BUILDARGS lift now maps usage.cache_read_input_tokens -> cached_tokens (single owner, covers all five Anthropic engines + streamed usage). cache_creation_input_tokens deliberately excluded. Gated by the existing engine-level Anthropic subtest in t/91_response_usage.t (real Engine::Anthropic->chat_response + mock body), no new fixture needed.

Orchestrator review 2026-09-01: diff 196a274 verified. BUILDARGS lift reads both spellings into lexicals (no autoviv), OpenAI shape wins if both present, cache_creation excluded. Note: the GAP comment right after the new assertion in t/91_response_usage.t is now stale (says no accessor exists) - handed to the k101 worker as a side cleanup. Closing.
